test_explicit_ids_route_home (tests.test_sc_avg_worthy_2026_11_26d.AvgWorthyRoutingTests.test_explicit_ids_route_home) ... PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-AVG-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. t603u's PoE table gives Groot as 'Witch → Necromancer (adapted)' while its section 6 says PoE 1 has no Druid starting class and 'I wouldn't force a perfect match where the game doesn't provide one.' Chosen default: Groot is recorded as NO_FORCED_MATCH in the PoE layer (the adapted row is kept as the paste's approximation, not as a mapping), while his Diablo II Druid match stands as interpretive. Second default in the same entry: the specialization-gate and party-composition invariants are readings under SC-AEP-001, not invariant classes.
