test_explicit_only_and_routes_home (tests.test_sc_tol_001_kernel.RoutingAndIsolationTests.test_explicit_only_and_routes_home) ... PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-TOL-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. t608u supplies the SC-TOL-001 design thread (v1, v2, v2.1-rc1, v2.1-rc2) and t609u names the attached rc5 as the version to implement. Chosen default: SC-TOL-001 is a structural compiler reference (gates T0-T8 as predicates over graph fixtures), SILVER, not an invariant class and not GOLD; rc5 is implemented with seven recorded kernel fixes rather than verbatim; delegation-chain verification stays permissive by default but unregistered hops are surfaced as QUALIFIED; rc6 (Shax t610u) closed two items: a failing child taints the parent's current compilation only (D1), and an empirically living system is LIVING_OBSERVED or SELF_MAINTENANCE_UNVERIFIED, never INERT (D2). rc7 (Shax t611u) reports a structural result, an epistemic result and a combined certification separately, keeping the rc6 propagation rule; its own provisional defaults (coverage limits count as structural QUALIFIED; NOT_EMPIRICAL ranks above UNVERIFIED; a child's structural FAIL makes the parent's structural result FAIL for the current compilation) are flagged. Alternatives remain open: make require_full_chain_verification the default; promote T8 into SCC-001-AC.
