PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-WOW-001 source=summon status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=top_compiled_match reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. The brief asks whether SC-TRIAD-001 (preservation, assimilation, transformation) fits Warcraft as Order/Void/Death or as Titans/Old Gods/Jailer. Chosen default: the triad fits on the consent axis, not on the cosmic-force axis. Assimilation is the Void (Old Gods' whispers, the Black Empire, Black Blood, Xal'atath's bargains). Preservation and transformation are stances found inside every force (the Titans order and also reserve a re-origination; Death judges and the Jailer remakes; the Light shelters and also coerces), so neither is assigned to one force. The Burning Legion is annihilation, the same fourth kind of outside party left open in SC-GOT-001.
PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-WOW-DF-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. Shax (t594u) reads Dragonflight as the good dragons spreading their wings against the bad ones, 'the good Tok'ra versus the bad ghouls' (Goa'uld). Canon puts consent violations on both sides: the Aspects took proto-dragon eggs from the wild to infuse with Order magic, and Neltharion bound the dracthyr with the Oathbinder; the Primal Incarnates refused the titans' gift, then killed, deceived and sold out to the Void. Chosen default: the Tok'ra/Goa'uld line runs through acts, not flights. Each act is classified as SC-SCC-001 does (COERCIVE, CONSENSUAL, UNKNOWN). The Old Gods' hold on Neltharion is the Goa'uld case; the Aspects' acceptance of the gift and Vyranoth's turn are the Tok'ra-type cases; Shax's good-versus-bad framing holds for the outcome of the arc and is kept as his interpretation.
PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-WOW-DF-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. Shax (t594u) reads Dragonflight as the good dragons spreading their wings against the bad ones, 'the good Tok'ra versus the bad ghouls' (Goa'uld). Canon puts consent violations on both sides: the Aspects took proto-dragon eggs from the wild to infuse with Order magic, and Neltharion bound the dracthyr with the Oathbinder; the Primal Incarnates refused the titans' gift, then killed, deceived and sold out to the Void. Chosen default: the Tok'ra/Goa'uld line runs through acts, not flights. Each act is classified as SC-SCC-001 does (COERCIVE, CONSENSUAL, UNKNOWN). The Old Gods' hold on Neltharion is the Goa'uld case; the Aspects' acceptance of the gift and Vyranoth's turn are the Tok'ra-type cases; Shax's good-versus-bad framing holds for the outcome of the arc and is kept as his interpretation.
