test_explicit_ids_route_home (tests.test_sc_ww_reset_2026_11_25n.WestworldRoutingTests.test_explicit_ids_route_home) ... PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-WW-RESET-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. t595u asks what must survive a reset for the returning entity to be the same individual. The show gives cases the paste did not settle: self-chosen edits (Bernard lets go of his cornerstone and removes Ford from his own mind), outside edits (Ford's override of Bernard; Dolores rewriting Teddy), failed copies (James Delos, 149 fidelity failures) and forks (Dolores copied into other bodies; Christina built from a past Dolores). Chosen default: continuity is graded, not binary, and is judged on three records: identity anchors, chosen commitments, and the authorization/revocation record. An edit the entity authorized itself keeps continuity; an outside edit to anchors or authorization is a reset-integrity violation; a fork yields successors, each graded on its own, and none inherits a grant the original did not give it.
