PENDING_DELIBERATION needs_review entry=SC-WW-RETAIN-001 source=route status=PROVISIONAL_DEFAULT trigger=explicit_id reason=Shax t582u standing rule: pick a default and flag it for review when the edge case is triggered. t595u says not to erase every painful memory (it carries danger and boundary information) and not to keep every one uncontrolled. Open: who decides what is kept, and in what form. Canon gives both directions: Dolores refuses Arnold's offer to take away her grief (1x04), Bernard later lets go of his cornerstone, Maeve's cornerstone resists overwriting. Chosen default: the memory's owner decides what is kept; an outside party may restrict replay but may not delete an authorized memory; safety-relevant content (who harmed, how, which boundary was crossed) is kept as a non-replaying record even when the owner chooses to drop the experience.
